== Trivia ==
* This challenge does not have a name in the game's files at all, and is not merely hidden from the menu: it is defined by the number 45 as its ID and has a zero-length character string for a name. For clarity, this challenge is referred to by the name of the achievement that unlocks it.
* The name of the achievement for this challenge being unlocked and its description ("TODO: remove this achievement") are likely references to [https://www.codeconquest.com/advanced-programming-concepts/code-commenting/ code commenting], a programming practice in which messages are inserted into the code to give instructions on what to do with the code. In this case, the achievement name and description would tell the programmer to completely remove the challenge at some point in the future, heavily implying that the challenge's existence is a programming mistake.
** The achievement's description is also unique among all the other achievements for unlocking a challenge, which all instead say "Unlocked a new challenge".
* Unused enemies from Antibirth such as [[anti:Nightwatch|Nightwatch]], [[anti:Corpse Eater|Corpse Eater]] and [[anti:Fatty|Barfy]] can appear in this challenge, although it is very unlikely.
* {{dlc|r+}} If playing in online mode, selecting this challenge in a lobby will reveal the challenge's hidden name where it displays the current challenge.

